{"title":"Bibliography and References","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Bibliography and References"},"headingText":"Primary Sources","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\n### Cambridge International Examinations\n\n- Cambridge Assessment International Education. (2023). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics 0625 Syllabus for Examination in 2026, 2027 and 2028*. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press & Assessment.\n\n- Cambridge Assessment International Education. (2023). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics 0625: Specimen Papers and Mark Schemes*. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press & Assessment.\n\n### Textbooks and Coursebooks\n\n- Sang, D., Jones, G., Chadha, G., & Woodside, R. (2021). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics Coursebook* (3rd Edition). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n- Sang, D., Jones, G., Chadha, G., & Woodside, R. (2021). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics Workbook* (3rd Edition). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n- Sang, D., Jones, G., Chadha, G., & Woodside, R. (2021). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics Teacher's Resource* (3rd Edition). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n## Supplementary Resources\n\n### Practical Work and Laboratory Guides\n\n- Association for Science Education. (2010). *The Language of Measurement*. Hatfield: ASE Publications.\n\n- CLEAPSS. (2019). *Laboratory Handbook and Hazcards*. Uxbridge: CLEAPSS.\n\n### Reference Works\n\n- Halliday, D., Resnick, R., & Walker, J. (2018). *Fundamentals of Physics* (11th Edition). Hoboken: John Wiley & Sons.\n\n- Tipler, P. A., & Mosca, G. (2018). *Physics for Scientists and Engineers* (7th Edition). New York: W. H. Freeman.\n\n### Online Resources\n\n- Cambridge International. (2023). *School Support Hub*. Available at: www.cambridgeinternational.org/support\n\n- PhET Interactive Simulations. (2023). *Physics Simulations*. University of Colorado Boulder. Available at: https://phet.colorado.edu/\n\n- BBC Bitesize. (2023). *GCSE Physics Revision*. Available at: www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize\n\n## Image and Media Credits\n\nAll diagrams, figures, and illustrations in this guide have been created specifically for this publication or are used under appropriate educational licenses.\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nThe author wishes to acknowledge the contributions of:\n\n- Cambridge Assessment International Education for providing the syllabus framework and examination standards\n- Physics educators worldwide whose teaching insights have informed the pedagogical approach\n- Students whose questions and challenges have helped shape the content and presentation\n- The open-source community for tools and resources that made this publication possible\n\n## Copyright and Permissions\n\nThis revision guide is intended for educational purposes. All rights to the Cambridge IGCSE Physics syllabus content remain with Cambridge Assessment International Education.\n\n---\n\n*This bibliography was compiled to ensure academic integrity and to provide students with additional resources for further study.*\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Primary Sources\n\n### Cambridge International Examinations\n\n- Cambridge Assessment International Education. (2023). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics 0625 Syllabus for Examination in 2026, 2027 and 2028*. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press & Assessment.\n\n- Cambridge Assessment International Education. (2023). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics 0625: Specimen Papers and Mark Schemes*. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press & Assessment.\n\n### Textbooks and Coursebooks\n\n- Sang, D., Jones, G., Chadha, G., & Woodside, R. (2021). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics Coursebook* (3rd Edition). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n- Sang, D., Jones, G., Chadha, G., & Woodside, R. (2021). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics Workbook* (3rd Edition). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n- Sang, D., Jones, G., Chadha, G., & Woodside, R. (2021). *Cambridge IGCSE Physics Teacher's Resource* (3rd Edition). Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n## Supplementary Resources\n\n### Practical Work and Laboratory Guides\n\n- Association for Science Education. (2010). *The Language of Measurement*. Hatfield: ASE Publications.\n\n- CLEAPSS. (2019). *Laboratory Handbook and Hazcards*. Uxbridge: CLEAPSS.\n\n### Reference Works\n\n- Halliday, D., Resnick, R., & Walker, J. (2018). *Fundamentals of Physics* (11th Edition). Hoboken: John Wiley & Sons.\n\n- Tipler, P. A., & Mosca, G. (2018). *Physics for Scientists and Engineers* (7th Edition). New York: W. H. Freeman.\n\n### Online Resources\n\n- Cambridge International. (2023). *School Support Hub*. Available at: www.cambridgeinternational.org/support\n\n- PhET Interactive Simulations. (2023). *Physics Simulations*. University of Colorado Boulder. Available at: https://phet.colorado.edu/\n\n- BBC Bitesize. (2023). *GCSE Physics Revision*. Available at: www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize\n\n## Image and Media Credits\n\nAll diagrams, figures, and illustrations in this guide have been created specifically for this publication or are used under appropriate educational licenses.\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nThe author wishes to acknowledge the contributions of:\n\n- Cambridge Assessment International Education for providing the syllabus framework and examination standards\n- Physics educators worldwide whose teaching insights have informed the pedagogical approach\n- Students whose questions and challenges have helped shape the content and presentation\n- The open-source community for tools and resources that made this publication possible\n\n## Copyright and Permissions\n\nThis revision guide is intended for educational purposes. All rights to the Cambridge IGCSE Physics syllabus content remain with Cambridge Assessment International Education.\n\n---\n\n*This bibliography was compiled to ensure academic integrity and to provide students with additional resources for further study.*\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":8,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"png","fig-dpi":96,"df